.\" offload(1) manpage — mdoc format
.Dd October 9, 2026
.Dt OFFLOAD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm offload
.Nd poka-yoke disk offload tool for macOS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -target-home Ar path
.Ar subcommand
.Op Ar args ...
.Op Fl -apply
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
moves heavy, low-velocity data out of
.Pa $HOME
onto an external drive. The home folder itself stays internal — we
move the
.Em contents
of specific paths inside
.Pa $HOME
and replace each with a symlink, or for archive targets leave a fresh
empty directory. This is the supported pattern: iCloud, FileVault,
login, and macOS updates remain untouched.
.Pp
A guard launcher refuses to start an app whose data lives on an
unmounted volume.
.Nm
is mistake-proof by design: dry-run is the default, signature
verification precedes every destructive step, and all operations are
idempotent.
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width 18n
.It Cm help
Print the embedded long-form documentation
.Pq the script header is the single source of truth .
.It Cm version
Print the script version.
.It Cm status
Disk space, summary of all targets, recent log entries, admin todo.
.It Cm drives Op Fl -benchmark
Scan
.Pa /Volumes/*
mount points, reporting filesystem, SSD, free space, backup
.Pq Time Machine, Backblaze ,
ownership, encryption, and role. Classify each as
.Sy HOT
.Pq external SSD ,
.Sy COLD
.Pq external spinner or HFS+ ,
.Sy EXCLUDED
.Pq Time Machine destination, internal, read-only ,
or
.Sy UNKNOWN .
Heuristics use
.Xr diskutil 8
fields
.Pq Solid State, Protocol, File System Personality, Device Location
and
.Xr tmutil 8
.Pq destinationinfo .
Prints a table plus a "Detected:" footer with the lines to add to
.Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/offload/offload.conf
so the user can persist the result manually
.Pq the command never writes the config file itself .
With
.Fl -benchmark ,
adds a timed
.Xr dd 1
read-speed column measured against each non-EXCLUDED drive
.Pq about 10s per drive .
The measurement is page-cache-aware on macOS — trust the relative
ordering between drives, not absolute MB/s figures.
.It Cm list Op Fl -all-users
Every entry in
.Va OFFLOAD_TARGETS
with its category, strategy, admin requirement, the bytes that would
be reclaimed by offloading it, and current state
.Pq on-disk , symlinked , archived , merged , absent , unreadable .
A potential-reclaim total is printed at the end. With
.Fl -all-users
.Pq list only ,
iterates every real macOS user account
.Pq UID >= 500, non-underscore-prefixed
and prints a section per user plus a grand total. Useful for the
Admin account auditing which homes still have movable data.
.It Cm plan
Advice only: how much the boot drive needs, where each target would
go, what is private, backup coverage, and priced options
.Pq buy hardware, cloud
for any shortfall. Nothing moves; nothing touches the network.
.It Cm prices Op Fl -update
Print the dated price table used by
.Cm plan .
.Fl -update
is the only network call
.Nm
makes, and only when asked.
.It Cm repos Op Fl -synced-ok
Every git repo under
.Pa ~/Documents/Projects
with a verdict: keep (active), synced (in a sync folder), reclone
(clean, pushed, cold), or move (cold but unsafe to remove).
.It Cm reclone Ar path | all Op Fl -apply
Restore recloned or moved repositories.
.It Cm restore Ar Label | path Op Fl -apply
Bring a cloud archive back.
.It Cm checklist
Generated progress checklist, live from OFFLOAD_TARGETS. Includes
exact commands to advance each entry.
.It Cm launch Ar BundleName
Guarded launch. Refuses with a macOS dialog if the app's symlinked
data directory points to an unmounted volume.
.It Cm move Ar Label Op Fl -apply Op Fl -synced-ok Op Fl -upload
Offload one entry by label. The
.Fl -synced-ok
flag permits moving repositories inside sync folders;
.Fl -upload
allows a cloud strategy to upload to an approved remote, only with
.Fl -apply .
.It Cm move Ar category Op Fl -apply
Offload every entry in a category. Categories:
.Cm app , home , cold , merge , dev , cache , sweep , repos , protected , vm , media-lib .
Default is dry-run; supply
.Fl -apply
to mutate.
.It Cm relocations Pq alias: Cm media-libraries
Print native-UI relocation steps for everything in
.Va OFFLOAD_TARGETS
with strategy
.Cm native-ui :
the VM disks of Docker Desktop, Colima and OrbStack, Photos Library,
Music.app library, iMovie / Final Cut libraries. We never auto-move
these because the apps cache absolute paths internally and the native
UIs handle the transition cleanly.
Colima has no such setting: its steps stop every VM, copy Colima's
.Pa _disks
folder with
.Ic cp -aH
and link the copy into place.
.Xr cp 1
keeps the disks sparse on an APFS drive, and
.Fl H
copies the disks themselves when
.Pa _disks
already links to another drive.
When
.Pa _disks
already resolves to
.Pa $OFFLOAD_HOT/Colima/_disks ,
it prints no Colima steps: that folder holds the live disks.
A VM disk is typically the biggest single win.
.It Cm protected Ar Label Op Fl -apply
Move a target flagged
.Va admin?=yes .
Requires
.Fl -target-home
pointing at a different user's home, admin-group caller, and FDA.
.It Cm drain Oo Ar name ... Oc Oo Fl -need Ar GiB Oc Op Fl -apply
Free space on a full HOT drive. Moves top-level entries of
.Va OFFLOAD_HOT
to
.Pa $OFFLOAD_COLD/Drained/<HOT name>/ ,
verifies file count and bytes, deletes the source, and leaves a symlink.
Without names it prints every movable entry by size and suggests the
fewest moves that reach
.Fl -need
(default 30 GiB free);
.Fl -apply
requires names. Never offers what offload owns on HOT, media libraries,
or a folder that holds a VM disk: Docker Desktop's data folder, Colima's
.Pa _disks
folder or the folder it links to, and OrbStack's data folder
.Pq its Va data_dir No setting, or where its default folder links .
Colima's
.Pa _disks
sits in
.Pa ~/.colima/_lima ,
or where
.Ev LIMA_HOME , COLIMA_HOME
or
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
moves it; the drain keeps
.Pa ~/.colima/_lima/_disks
too.
The physical path decides, so a symlink into HOT counts.
When a VM's folder is the HOT root itself, the drain keeps every entry
there.
A full host volume makes a sparse VM disk such as Docker Desktop's
.Pa Docker.raw
fail every VM write with an input/output error.
.El
.Sh DATA MODEL
Every relocatable thing is a row in
.Va OFFLOAD_TARGETS .
Every subcommand reads from this list; there is no parallel
hardcoded knowledge. Schema is pipe-delimited:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
label | category | source | dest | strategy | admin? | bundle
.Ed
.Pp
Tokens expanded at runtime:
.Bl -tag -width 12n
.It Sy <TH>
.Pa $TARGET_HOME
.Pq current user's $HOME by default .
.It Sy <TARGET_HOME>
Same as
.Sy <TH>
.Pq older configs .
.It Sy <U>
basename of
.Pa $TARGET_HOME .
.It Sy <DATE>
YYYY-MM-DD.
.It Sy HOT/
Prefix —
.Ev $OFFLOAD_HOT/ ,
else an SSD in
.Ev OFFLOAD_DRIVES .
.It Sy COLD/
Prefix —
.Ev $OFFLOAD_COLD/ ,
else a spinner in
.Ev OFFLOAD_DRIVES .
.It Sy CLOUD/
Prefix — first rclone remote in
.Ev OFFLOAD_APPROVED_REMOTES .
.El
.Pp
For symlink and archive rows, the drive is picked at move time: the
first mounted, eligible drive that keeps
.Ev OFFLOAD_HEADROOM
free after the move. Network mounts, ExFAT and removable sticks never
qualify; private labels require an encrypted volume with ownership on.
An attached encrypted sparsebundle counts as an encrypted drive, unless
its file sits on the boot drive.
.Pp
Strategies:
.Bl -tag -width 14n
.It Cm symlink
rsync to dest, verify file count and bytes, rm source, ln -s dest source.
.It Cm archive
rsync to dest, rm source, recreate empty source. No symlink — fresh
empty target for new arrivals
.Pq Pa ~/Downloads .
.It Cm merge
rsync
.Fl -update
into existing dest, rm source. Dest is authoritative; source is gone.
.It Cm sweep
.Xr find 1
subdirs matching internal patterns
.Pq node_modules , .venv , target , build , dist , __pycache__ , .next
and delete. No destination; data is rebuildable from source.
.It Cm purge
Delete the source directory entirely, then recreate it empty. For
caches and rebuild-on-demand support files
.Pq iOS DeviceSupport , ~/.cache , ~/.npm , Homebrew cache .
Apps re-populate the dir as needed.
.It Cm native-ui
Printed instructions only. The tool never auto-mutates media
libraries.
.It Cm repos
Cold git repos: clean, pushed repos get a verified
.Ic git bundle --all
on COLD, a manifest line, then go (the remote is the archive); unsafe
repos are copied whole to COLD, verified, then removed.
.Fl -apply
re-checks the remote first. Repos in sync folders need
.Fl -synced-ok .
.It Cm cloud
.Xr rclone 1
copy to an approved remote, check (cryptcheck for crypt), record,
remove. Only with
.Fl -apply -upload .
.El
.Pp
Categories:
.Cm app , home , cold , merge , dev , cache , sweep , repos , protected , vm , media-lib .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width 22n
.It Fl -target-home Ar path
Operate on a different user's home. Triggers admin-mode invariants
for
.Cm move
and
.Cm protected :
caller must NOT be the target user, must be in the
.Cm admin
group, and (for protected targets) Terminal must have Full Disk Access.
.Cm list
honors
.Fl -target-home
without admin gating (read-only).
Defaults to
.Pa $HOME .
.It Fl -benchmark
.Cm drives
only. Run a 1 GB
.Xr dd 1
read against each non-EXCLUDED drive and report rough MB/s. Cache-
aware on macOS; useful for comparing drives, not absolute capacity.
Adds about 10 seconds per drive. Probe files
.Pq Pa .offload-benchmark-probe-1g
are left on each drive for reproducible re-runs.
.It Fl -all-users
.Cm list
only. Iterate every real macOS user account and emit per-user
sections plus a grand-total potential reclaim. POSIX permissions on
.Pa /Users/<other>/Library
.Pq mode 700
block one user from reading another's contents; rows the caller
cannot read are marked
.Sy unreadable
with no reclaim figure, and a hint at the bottom of the output
suggests:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo offload --target-home /Users/<other> list
.Ed
.Pp
Running
.Cm list
under
.Cm sudo
is supported and safe; it is read-only and does not violate the
"never sudo from inside" invariant
.Pq the script itself never invokes sudo .
.It Fl -apply
Actually mutate. Without it, every operation is a dry-run that
prints intent only.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Drive paths come from environment variables
.Ev OFFLOAD_HOT
and
.Ev OFFLOAD_COLD ,
or from a config file at
.Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/offload/offload.conf .
The config file is parsed, never run. It accepts comments,
.Cm KEY="value"
lines and
.Cm KEY=( ... )
or
.Cm KEY+=( ... )
lists of quoted rows; anything else is an error, so a typo cannot
run as a command:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
OFFLOAD_HOT=/Volumes/MyFastSSD
OFFLOAD_COLD=/Volumes/MyArchiveHDD
# optional: extend (+=) or replace (=) OFFLOAD_TARGETS
OFFLOAD_TARGETS+=(
  "MyCustom|app|<TH>/Library/Application Support/Custom|HOT/MovedAppData/<U>/Custom|symlink|no|MyCustom"
)
.Ed
.Pp
Optional keys:
.Bl -tag -width 30n
.It Ev OFFLOAD_DRIVES
Additional opt-in drives for
.Sy HOT/
or
.Sy COLD/ .
.It Ev OFFLOAD_HEADROOM
Percent a drive keeps free after a move.
.It Ev OFFLOAD_BOOT_FREE_PCT
Plan's target for the boot drive.
.It Ev OFFLOAD_PRIVATE_LABELS
Private labels; defaults to Signal, Messages, Keybase, and iOS-Backups.
.It Ev OFFLOAD_REPO_KEEP
Repos never recloned; glob on path or name.
.It Ev OFFLOAD_APPROVED_REMOTES
Approved rclone remotes for
.Sy CLOUD/ .
.El
.Pp
Environment variables:
.Ev OFFLOAD_HOT ,
.Ev OFFLOAD_COLD ,
.Ev OFFLOAD_HEADROOM ,
.Ev OFFLOAD_CONF ,
.Ev OFFLOAD_REPO_COLD_DAYS ,
.Ev OFFLOAD_ALLOW_PLAINTEXT ,
and
.Ev OFFLOAD_PRICES_URL .
.Ev OFFLOAD_VOLUMES
and
.Ev OFFLOAD_BZINFO
point the drive scan elsewhere (tests).
.Ev OFFLOAD_REPO_COLD_DAYS
defaults to 90.
.Ev OFFLOAD_ALLOW_PLAINTEXT Ns =1
lets private data land on a plain drive, at the user's risk.
.Pp
For backward compatibility with v0.1.x, configs that still declare
.Va OFFLOAD_APPS
get auto-converted into
.Va OFFLOAD_TARGETS
rows for any labels not already present.
.Sh DESIGN
.Nm
follows poka-yoke discipline: bad outcomes are structurally
prevented, not merely documented.
.Bl -enum
.It
.Sy Single source of truth.
.Va OFFLOAD_TARGETS
is read by every subcommand. No duplicated copies.
.It
.Sy Dry-run by default.
Mutation requires
.Fl -apply .
.It
.Sy Verify before delete.
Cross-volume moves rsync to destination, compare file count + total
bytes, remove source only on signature match.
.It
.Sy Idempotent.
Re-running on an already-symlinked source skips. Existing
destinations are never silently overwritten.
.It
.Sy Never sudo from inside.
EACCES paths append to
.Pa ~/offload-admin-todo.txt
and a reviewable wrapper is emitted at
.Pa ~/bin/offload-admin-pass .
.It
.Sy Two-account workflow.
Targets flagged
.Va admin?=yes
require a separate Admin account whose Terminal has Full Disk Access.
.It
.Sy Guard launcher.
.Cm offload launch
checks the symlink target before opening the app.
.It
.Sy Every drive weighed.
A move goes to a drive that is mounted, fit for the data, and keeps
headroom; a run never promises the same free space twice. Private data
never lands in plaintext.
.It
.Sy Network only when asked.
.Cm plan
and
.Cm prices
are advice; the only calls out are
.Cm prices --update
and a
.Sy CLOUD/
move run with
.Fl -apply -upload
to a remote the team approved.
.El
.Ss DOES NOT
.Bl -bullet
.It
Relocate
.Pa $HOME
via
.Cm dscl . -change NFSHomeDirectory .
That breaks iCloud Drive, confuses FileVault, and has been broken by
multiple macOS updates. We move
.Em contents ,
not the pointer.
.It
Symlink Apple sandbox containers
.Pq Pa ~/Library/Containers/com.apple.* .
The sandbox refuses to follow.
.It
Symlink browser profiles
.Pq Sy Chrome , Firefox , Brave , Zen .
Constant SQLite writes cause corruption.
.It
Auto-move media libraries (Photos / Music / iMovie / Final Cut).
Use
.Cm offload media-libraries
for the native-UI steps.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss First-time setup
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mkdir -p ~/.config/offload
cat > ~/.config/offload/offload.conf <<EOF
OFFLOAD_HOT=/Volumes/MyFastSSD
OFFLOAD_COLD=/Volumes/MyArchiveHDD
EOF
.Ed
.Ss Inspect everything
.Bd -literal -offset indent
offload status
offload list
offload checklist
.Ed
.Ss Safe first sweep
.Bd -literal -offset indent
offload move BuildCruft
offload move BuildCruft --apply
.Ed
.Ss Move one app or an entire category
.Bd -literal -offset indent
offload move Signal --apply
offload move app    --apply
offload move home   --apply
.Ed
.Ss Guarded launch
.Bd -literal -offset indent
offload launch Signal
.Ed
.Ss A full HOT drive
.Bd -literal -offset indent
offload drain                  # plan: movable entries, sizes
offload drain ROMs --apply     # move to COLD, symlink back
.Ed
.Ss Media libraries (native UI; not scripted)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
offload media-libraries
.Ed
.Ss Where things could go, and what it would cost
.Bd -literal -offset indent
offload drives                 # every volume, backup, encryption
offload plan                   # advice only
offload repos                  # git repo verdicts
offload move Repos             # dry run; then --apply
.Ed
.Ss Admin running on another user's home
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# logged in as Admin account, Terminal has FDA
offload protected --target-home /Users/alice Messages --apply
offload --target-home /Users/alice move Signal --apply
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width 36n
.It Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/offload/offload.conf
User configuration: drive paths and
.Va OFFLOAD_TARGETS
overrides/extensions.
.It Pa ~/offload-YYYY-MM-DD.log
Per-run log, append-only.
.It Pa ~/offload-admin-todo.txt
Paths collected at run time when an operation failed with EACCES.
.It Pa ~/bin/offload-admin-pass
Emitted sudo-review script (only created when admin todo is non-empty).
.It Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/offload/prices.tsv
Price rows; user rows override by id.
.It Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/offload/reclone.tsv
Manifest of recloned and moved repositories, and of cloud archives.
.It Pa <COLD>/offload/Repos/<user>/
Repository bundles, moved repositories, and manifest copy.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Invariant violation, invalid input, or fatal error.
.It 2
Destination conflict; manual review required.
.It 3
Permission denied; an admin pass is needed (see
.Pa ~/bin/offload-admin-pass ) .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rsync 1 ,
.Xr tmutil 8 ,
.Xr diskutil 8 ,
.Xr dd 1 ,
.Xr ln 1 ,
.Xr launchctl 1
.Pp
For cross-drive deduplication, consider installing
.Xr jdupes 1
.Pq Cm brew install jdupes .
Future versions of
.Nm
may integrate it directly; for now it is a separate tool.
.Sh AUTHORS
Maintained in the Sage-is/homebrew-apps tap.
Bug reports:
.Lk https://github.com/Sage-is/homebrew-apps/issues
.Sh BUGS
The script never invokes
.Cm sudo
itself. Some user-space paths require elevated privileges to move;
those are captured in
.Pa ~/offload-admin-todo.txt
and emitted as a separate sudo-review script for manual execution.
This is intentional.
